# ci/module-aliases.stock515 - stock 5.4 module name -> what 5.15 calls it
#
# The stock /vendor/lib/modules/modules.load is a 5.4 list.  Several entries
# were renamed between 5.4 and 5.15, so a plain name comparison reports them as
# missing when the driver is in fact present.  Each mapping below is a measured
# rename, not a guess: the left side was read from the device's own modules.load
# over adb, the right side comes from the 5.15 tree's KO_MODULE_NAME.
#
# Format:  <stock name>:<our name>
# A value of "-" means "no 5.15 module; handled another way", with the reason.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# mali_kbase -> mali_gondul
#   5.4 shipped the GPU as drivers/misc/mali_kbase.  5.15 moved it out of tree
#   to kernel_modules/kernel5.15/gpu/gondul/mali, whose Kbuild sets
#   "obj-$(CONFIG_MALI_MIDGARD) += mali_gondul.o" and whose Kbuild self-defaults
#   CONFIG_MALI_MIDGARD to m.  Same driver, new name.
#
# gnss_common_ctl_all -> unisoc_gnss_common_ctl_all
#   5.15's KO_MODULE_NAME for wcn/gnss/unisoc_gnss/gnss_common_ctl is
#   unisoc_gnss_common_ctl_all; the stock 5.4 name had no unisoc_ prefix.
#
# omnivision_td4160 -> omnivision_tcm + in-tree DSI panel driver
#   The 5.4 tree had a standalone omnivision_td4160.ko for this panel.  5.15
#   splits it: the panel itself is handled by the in-tree
#   drivers/unisoc_platform/sprd_disp DSI panel code (sprd_dsi_panel.c lists
#   td4160), and the touch controller is the out-of-tree
#   touchscreen/odm/omnivision_tcm unit, which builds as omnivision_tcm-modules.
#   NOT yet confirmed that the live touch node binds to omnivision_tcm on this
#   board -- flagged rather than claimed.
#
# wcn_bsp -> wcn_bsp
#   Not a rename, recorded to prevent a false alarm: the stock list's wcn_bsp.ko
#   is built IN TREE from drivers/unisoc_platform/sprdwcn (CONFIG_UNISOC_WCN_BSP),
#   so it appears in modules-intree.  kernel_modules also carries a copy of this
#   driver, but it builds as "unisoc_wcn_bsp", which nothing references.  The
#   in-tree one is authoritative because sprd_wlan_combo depends on "wcn_bsp".
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
mali_kbase:mali_gondul
gnss_common_ctl_all:unisoc_gnss_common_ctl_all
omnivision_td4160:omnivision_tcm-modules
wcn_bsp:wcn_bsp
